<%# Feed-card "more options" menu — Hoojah 2026 (redesign Phase 1, Task 1.3), mockup
    ~217-224's single `more-vertical` trigger. Before this task the card carried a bare
    `share-2` icon (`hujahs/_share_menu`'s own trigger) and no flag control at all; the
    mockup shows one glyph, so this partial is the feed card's OWN combined trigger —
    the show page keeps its separate share (`share-2`) + "More actions" (`more-horizontal`)
    pair untouched, because that screen renders its own header, not `_hujah_header`, and
    `spec/system/share_spec.rb` / `spec/system/flag_spec.rb` exercise it directly by
    aria-label.

    The six share intent links + native-share button below are the same markup
    `_share_menu` renders (WhatsApp/X/Telegram/Reddit/Facebook/Email), duplicated rather
    than shared because `_share_menu` bundles its own `<details>` around them and
    splitting that partial is out of scope for this task. The share TEXT is byte-identical
    to `_share_menu`'s — this IS the share payload `share_spec` and `_share_menu`'s own
    header call "the only place Hoojah shouts in caps".

    The URL, however, is NOT identical since issue #31: the feed deliberately shares the
    CANONICAL `hujah_url` here, not the `/s/:code` short link the show page's `_share_menu`
    now emits. That is a load-bearing choice, not drift — `ShortLink.for(hujah)` is a
    `find_or_create_by!`, i.e. a write-on-GET, and this menu renders on EVERY feed card,
    so calling it per card would be a feed N+1 that this codebase's N+1 discipline forbids.
    Short links are applied only on single-item share surfaces (the hoojah show page and
    the debate verdict), where it is one cheap idempotent query per page.

    `data-controller="share"` and the three `data-share-*-value` attributes stay on THIS
    `<details>` — share_controller.js reads them off its nearest `data-controller="share"`
    ancestor, so the native-share button inside this panel needs them here, not on
    `_share_menu`'s (which the feed no longer renders).

    The flag row is `hujahs/_flag_dialog` unmodified — it is already a self-contained
    unit (its own `data-controller="dialog"` scope, its own POST), designed to be
    embedded as one menu row, exactly how `hujahs/show` uses it today.

    Locals: hujah. %>
<% share_url = hujah_url(hujah.slug) %>
<% share_text = "\"#{strip_tags(hujah.body)} (by @#{hujah.user.username})\" Do you AGREE? NEUTRAL? DISAGREE?" %>
<% share_title = "Hoojah by @#{hujah.user.username}" %>

<details class="relative shrink-0"
         data-controller="share"
         data-share-title-value="<%= share_title %>"
         data-share-text-value="<%= share_text %>"
         data-share-url-value="<%= share_url %>">
  <summary class="list-none cursor-pointer text-faint" aria-label="More options">
    <%= lucide_icon("more-vertical", class: "w-5 h-5") %>
  </summary>
  <%= render layout: "ui/menu", locals: {width: "w-52"} do %>
    <h6 class="text-xs text-grey px-3 pb-1">Share this hoojah via</h6>

    <%# Native OS share sheet — hidden until the share controller confirms support. %>
    <button type="button" hidden
            data-share-target="button"
            data-action="share#share"
            class="<%= ds_menu_item_classes %> border-0 bg-transparent cursor-pointer">
      Share…
    </button>

    <%= link_to "WhatsApp", "https://wa.me/?text=#{CGI.escape("#{share_text} #{share_url}")}", target: "_blank", rel: "noopener", class: ds_menu_item_classes %>
    <%= link_to "X", "https://x.com/intent/tweet?url=#{CGI.escape(share_url)}&text=#{CGI.escape(share_text)}&via=hoojah_my", target: "_blank", rel: "noopener", class: ds_menu_item_classes %>
    <%= link_to "Telegram", "https://t.me/share/url?url=#{CGI.escape(share_url)}&text=#{CGI.escape(share_text)}", target: "_blank", rel: "noopener", class: ds_menu_item_classes %>
    <%= link_to "Reddit", "https://www.reddit.com/submit?url=#{CGI.escape(share_url)}&title=#{CGI.escape(share_text)}", target: "_blank", rel: "noopener", class: ds_menu_item_classes %>
    <%= link_to "Facebook", "https://www.facebook.com/sharer/sharer.php?u=#{CGI.escape(share_url)}", target: "_blank", rel: "noopener", class: ds_menu_item_classes %>
    <%= mail_to "hello@rudzainy.com", "Email", subject: share_title, body: "#{share_text}\n\n#{share_url}", class: ds_menu_item_classes %>

    <%= render "ui/divider", class: "my-1" %>
    <%# Slice 1: owner-only edit entry on the feed card, shown only while the body is
        editable (15-min window, no conviction). Same target as the show-page menu. %>
    <% if user_signed_in? && hujah.user_id == current_user.id && hujah.body_editable? %>
      <%= link_to "Edit hoojah", edit_hujah_path(hujah.slug), class: ds_menu_item_classes %>
    <% end %>
    <% if user_signed_in? %>
      <%= render "hujahs/flag_dialog", hujah: hujah %>
    <% else %>
      <%= link_to new_user_session_path,
            class: "#{ds_menu_item_classes(tone: "neutral")} flex items-center gap-1" do %>
        <%= lucide_icon("flag", class: "w-4 h-4") %> Login to flag this hoojah
      <% end %>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>
</details>
